{"chunk_id": "a7e824a9b390", "text": "This section narrates the climactic end of the Ramayana war. Enraged by his son\u2019s death, Ravana rides into battle and unleashes terrifying illusions, multiplying demons and even creating false forms of Rama and Lakshmana. Rama counters the magic and, aided by Matali who brings Indra\u2019s celestial chariot, confronts Ravana directly. After a fierce exchange of weapons, Rama invokes the Brahmastra and annihilates Ravana utterly. The gods rejoice, and Vibhishana becomes king of Lanka. Yet the victory turns emotionally harsh when Rama, fearing dishonor, rejects Sita because she lived in Ravana\u2019s captivity. Sita collapses in grief and proclaims her purity before the cosmic elements. The gods\u2014including Brahma, Agni, and Vayu\u2014testify to her innocence, explaining that Ravana could not violate her. Rama accepts her again, the slain monkeys are revived, Hanuman receives a blessing, and the heroes prepare to return to Ayodhya.\nRama slays Ravana with the Brahma weapon, Sita proves her purity before the gods, and Rama is reunited with her as the celestials celebrate.\nThemes: final battle, divine intervention, purity and honor, illusion and warfare, restoration and reunion", "vector": [0.011148260906338692, -0.017745938152074814, -0.01718214899301529, 0.0023038173094391823, -0.015839792788028717, 0.00805413257330656, -0.025477904826402664, -0.013631618581712246, -0.03133057430386543, -0.01818891428411007, 0.011061008088290691, 0.018135221675038338, 0.010705283842980862, 0.006607744377106428, -0.001495887292549014, 0.014739061705768108, 0.03589458391070366, -0.013504095375537872, 0.03052516095340252, -0.01622907631099224, 0.008611209690570831, -0.009416623041033745, -0.011732186190783978, 0.013745718635618687, -0.022417334839701653, -0.0080339964479208, 0.023007970303297043, -0.03393474221229553, 0.02792099118232727, -0.0008146418840624392, -0.010638166218996048, -0.025585293769836426, -0.009134728461503983, 0.002043735